<p>Stage and deduplicate policy transaction data from XML-flattened source tables, then merge into a downstream mart table. The script transforms raw policy and account data, ensures the latest record per policy and transaction date is selected, and performs an upsert into the target.</p>

<h3>High-Level Flow</h3>
<ul>
<li>Execute dependent notebook <code>staging_transformations_logic</code> to create temporary views <code>vw_policy_xml_raw</code> and <code>vw_account_xml_raw</code>.</li>
<li>Query the temporary views via Spark SQL to join policy and account data, applying type casting and a conditional logic for <code>is_fully_earned_ind</code>.</li>
<li>Apply a window function to deduplicate records, keeping only the most recent entry per <code>policy_number</code> and <code>transaction_effective_date</code> based on <code>load_ts</code>.</li>
<li>Create a temporary view <code>vw_policy_transaction_stage</code> from the deduplicated DataFrame.</li>
<li>Execute a SQL MERGE statement to insert new records or update existing ones in the target table <code>mart.policy_transaction</code>.</li>
</ul>

