<h3>Recent Change Summary</h3>
<p>The precision of the <code>written_premium</code> field was increased from <code>DECIMAL(18,3)</code> to <code>DECIMAL(18,6)</code> in the staging SQL SELECT statement. This change allows for higher fractional precision in the written premium amount during the initial data extraction and casting.</p>

<h3>Jira Story Traceability</h3>
<p>No Jira story references are present in the provided code or commit context.</p>

<h3>Risks / Follow-ups</h3>
<p><strong>Data Type Inconsistency:</strong> The <code>premium_change_amt</code> calculation still uses <code>DECIMAL(18,3)</code> casting for subtraction, while <code>written_premium</code> is now <code>DECIMAL(18,6)</code>. This may cause truncation or rounding differences between the stored premium and the calculated change amount.</p>
<p><strong>Undefined Variables in CASE:</strong> The CASE expression uses literals <code>Y</code> and <code>N</code> without quotes, which are likely intended as string literals <code>'Y'</code> and <code>'N'</code>. This will cause a syntax or runtime error (NameError) as <code>Y</code> and <code>N</code> are not defined.</p>
<p><strong>Missing Producer Code in MERGE:</strong> The column <code>producer_code</code> is selected in the staging query but is not included in the MERGE statement's UPDATE or INSERT column lists. This data will be lost and not persisted to the target table.</p>
