<h3>Risks / Follow-ups</h3>
<p><strong>Syntax Error in CASE Expression:</strong> The CASE expression uses unquoted literals <code>Y</code> and <code>N</code> (lines 24-26). These are likely intended to be strings <code>'Y'</code> and <code>'N'</code>. This will cause a runtime error (AnalysisException) due to unresolved column references.<br><strong>Missing Column in INSERT:</strong> The MERGE INSERT clause omits <code>account_number</code> and <code>producer_code</code>, while the UPDATE clause includes <code>account_number</code>. This creates an inconsistency; new records will not have an <code>account_number</code> populated.<br><strong>Data Type Inconsistency:</strong> The <code>premium_change_amt</code> is calculated using <code>DECIMAL(18,3)</code> casting, but the updated <code>written_premium</code> is <code>DECIMAL(18,6)</code>. This may lead to unintended precision loss or calculation mismatches.</p>
